[#:seon.task{:name "an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form"
             :intent "`seon.edit/single-form?` throws instead of answering false: `(seon.edit/single-form? \"{:a 1 :b}\")` throws IllegalArgumentException \"No value supplied for key: :b\" against its own `:boolean` output (observed in the JVM on default 6299bcda4). rewrite-clj parses the odd map without complaint, and `rewrite-clj.zip/sexpr` inside `seon.edit/location-sexpr` throws; `seon.edit/valid-form-operation?` therefore throws on a form-edit request whose replacement source holds an odd map anywhere, nested ones included. A map literal with an odd number of forms is not readable, so the answer is false and a form edit refuses it as unreadable source. Related, same owner: `(seon.edit/single-form? \"#_x (a)\")` answers false although the source holds one semantic form, because `seon.edit/single-form` counts `#_` nodes (`rewrite-clj.zip/right` skips only whitespace and comments); counting only `rewrite-clj.zip/sexpr-able?` nodes would make it true, but `seon.edit/single-form` would then replace with the `(a)` node alone and drop `#_x`, so decide both at `seon.edit/single-form`. Read `seon.edit/single-form`, `seon.edit/location-sexpr` and `seon.edit/parse-root`."}]
